{"_comment":"Fake token shapes read by the Node.js and the Python secret tests. Each entry is a list of segments joined into one text: a literal string, {\"rep\": [unit, times]} (the unit repeated) or {\"alpha\": [n, offset]} (n characters of the cycling alphabet 0-9a-zA-Z from the offset, so the body has mixed characters but is no real credential). \"expect\" is the secret type the text must give (GITHUB_TOKEN, AWS_KEY, AWS_SECRET, SLACK_TOKEN, STRIPE_KEY, JWT, PRIVATE_KEY) or \"none\". Nothing here is a real credential.","alphabet":"0123456789abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ","entries":[
